# Drafting workflow

Ripul researches on his own, pastes links and notes into the agent, and
asks for **drafts** — not finished publish-ready copy without review.

## When Ripul says "draft a post" (or similar)

1. **Read what he provided** — URLs, excerpts, bullet notes, his angle.
   Do not invent sources, quotes, or facts not in the thread.
2. **Pick the post type** — `linked` | `essay` | `notes` | `review` (see
   `content.mdc`). Default to `linked` when the prompt is mostly a URL.
3. **Ask only if blocked** — missing attribution, unclear stance, or
   whether it's a link post vs essay. One focused question beats five.
4. **Output a draft** as MDX frontmatter + body, ready for
   `src/content/posts/` once the Astro site exists. Until then, output
   full markdown in the chat.
5. **Match `writing-style.mdc`** — sharp, short, DF-style. Ripul edits
   voice; you supply structure and a strong first pass.

## Frontmatter template

```yaml
---
title: "Sharp Title Here"
description: "One-line meta summary for search and AI (optional; auto-generated if omitted)"
date: 2026-05-25T20:00:00Z
# include time so newest posts sort to top deterministically
type: linked          # essay | linked | notes | review
tags: [apple, legal]
star: false           # true only for type: essay (originals)
linkUrl: "https://…"  # required when type: linked
linkAuthor: "Name"    # optional
---
```

## Link-post draft checklist

- [ ] Title is a take, not a summary
- [ ] Attribution in the first lines
- [ ] Exactly one blockquote (the best line from the source)
- [ ] Commentary adds opinion — does not repeat the quote
- [ ] No invented quotes; paraphrase only what's in Ripul's notes if
      he didn't paste the exact line

## Essay draft checklist

- [ ] `star: true` and `★` will appear on the published title
- [ ] Thesis in paragraph one
- [ ] Paragraphs mostly 1–3 sentences
- [ ] No "Welcome to…" or throat-clearing

## After the draft

- Offer a **tighter** alternate title if one is obviously stronger.
- Do not push publish, SEO, or social copy unless asked.
- If Ripul gives a contrary angle mid-thread, rewrite — don't argue.
